WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.207
- Okay, I'm back with

00:00:01.207 --> 00:00:03.400
soon-to-be rockstar
Salem (audience cheers)

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.160
and sitting in with my band y'all all day

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.490
has been legendary drummer Sheila E.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.380
She's joining me over
on the couch right now.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.265
What's up, Sheila?

00:00:11.265 --> 00:00:12.530
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.363
- I'm so good.

00:00:13.363 --> 00:00:14.430
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.530
I said this in rehearsals,

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.590
we're so honored to have you.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.440
You look like a total rock goddess

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.273
and your outfit.

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:20.106
I love you!

00:00:20.106 --> 00:00:20.939
- Thank you.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:21.772
- So how's it going with my band?

00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:22.870
Are they keeping up with you?

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.640
- They're not bad for a bunch of guys.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.696
No, just kidding. (laughs)

00:00:25.696 --> 00:00:26.529
(Kelly laughs and people clap)

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:27.563
- I love Sheila.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.830
Well, thank you again,

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.475
I mean, just for, for coming, for

00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:33.462
♪ Regular rock ♪

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:35.879
(rock music)

00:00:37.676 --> 00:00:38.509
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:39.342
You're gonna keep doing it

00:00:39.342 --> 00:00:41.690
'cause it brings me joy.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.971
So you heard me ask John like

00:00:43.971 --> 00:00:46.010
what rock music means to him?

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.100
Like what about you?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.507
Like when you think of someone say,

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:50.610
"Oh, you're, you're a rock star."

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.230
Like, what does that mean?

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.580
- Wow, interesting

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.580
because you know,

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.700
music has evolved so much,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.230
you know, from the beginning of

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.610
what was rock and roll, I mean.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.420
But it's, to me it's R&amp;B,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.253
it's country.

00:01:02.253 --> 00:01:04.750
I mean, I agree with a lot of
the things that he has said

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.470
you know, it's real,

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.633
it's heartfelt, you know,

00:01:09.594 --> 00:01:11.145
and I always want to be in a rock band.

00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:12.030
I always wanted to play,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.510
be the girl drummer in a rock band.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.190
It's like one of the
things on my bucket list.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.770
And, and it was interesting because

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.390
at one point I didn't want to be Sheila E,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.260
the leader anymore.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.093
I was like,

00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:24.926
I want to go play drums

00:01:24.926 --> 00:01:25.759
and I told Prince.

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:27.310
I said, "I'm going to go play drums

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.170
with some other people.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.200
I just want to play rock"

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.360
and he say, "you want to start a band?"

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.840
and we did Sign o' the Times

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:32.694
and I was like

00:01:32.694 --> 00:01:34.370
♪ Now playing drums ♪

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:35.820
Yeah, I love it.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.650
So rock and roll to me is just like,

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.680
you know passion.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.820
It's, it's heartfelt.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.790
It's R&amp;B.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:41.623
It's blues.

00:01:41.623 --> 00:01:42.456
It's everything.

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:43.550
- I know, I agree too.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:44.650
There's so many emotions in it.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.820
It can be very sweet.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.653
It can be...

00:01:47.653 --> 00:01:48.486
you know, Wild Horses,

00:01:48.486 --> 00:01:50.140
it could be something very sexy.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.870
It can be, it can be so many emotions.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.630
I think it's just, you gotta be all in.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.400
So what initially got
you into music though,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.233
cause I know it runs,

00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:58.210
It's your family right?
- Yeah.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.980
My dad, Pete Escovedo,
legendary percussionist.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:01.813
Amazing.

00:02:01.813 --> 00:02:04.180
Still playing and actually
we played last week

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.630
for breast cancers,

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.870
raising money last week.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:07.703
So it was good

00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:08.800
we're still playing together.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.810
My daddy.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.450
Yes. He's so awesome.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.020
He's 85 now and he's
still killing the game.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:14.853
He's amazing. (audience claps)

00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:16.280
- I love that.
- Yeah.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.400
- I love that.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.010
So what did you think,

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.610
cause you mentioned Prince a minute ago

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.333
and what did you think the
first time you met Prince?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.033
- Well, it's interesting

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.080
cause my dad at the time in the seventies,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.570
I met Prince in '77.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.560
My dad was with Santana at the time,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.510
my dad and my uncle,

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.770
they played with Santana.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.127
And my dad came home and said,

00:02:34.127 --> 00:02:35.890
"There's this young kid in the studio,

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.120
in the same studio as us.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.160
And like, he's playing
all the instruments,

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.430
he's producing and is incredible.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.263
His name is Prince."

00:02:42.263 --> 00:02:43.096
So it was like,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.850
I want to come by the studio, daddy.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:45.683
And he is like,

00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:46.516
"No, we're working,

00:02:46.516 --> 00:02:47.349
you can't come."

00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:48.239
So anyway,
- Boo.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:49.270
- (laughs) I know.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.350
So next you know,

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.300
I went to his concert the first time.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.010
So I went backstage to say hello

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.030
and he was combing his hair

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.850
and he saw me and he's like, "Hi."

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:57.683
And I said,

00:02:57.683 --> 00:02:58.516
"Oh, I want to introduce myself."

00:02:58.516 --> 00:02:59.540
He said, "I already know who you are.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.373
I'm a fan,

00:03:00.373 --> 00:03:01.206
I'm following you.

00:03:01.206 --> 00:03:02.180
You're amazing."
- What?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.580
- Yeah, cause he saw me
playing drums on television

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.590
and like
- That's amazing!

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.700
- Yeah, was really cool.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.650
And I, so we exchanged
numbers and that was it.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.890
That was the beginning of like

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.170
a long, forever relationship.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.820
- I mean an amazing one.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.310
Well, Salem, do you have
a question for Sheila?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.470
- I do actually.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.070
So I just really want to know like

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.810
who inspired you to play drums

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:24.400
and song write and do all this stuff?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.170
- My dad did and being around my family.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.770
My dad being a percussion player,

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.370
we had a lot of amazing musicians

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.390
come to the house all the time.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.520
So there were jam sessions.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.010
We would sit down and play.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.500
I watch my dad play a lot.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.483
The first time I played with my dad,

00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:40.980
I was five.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.600
But I wanted to be a track star.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.730
I was running track.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.170
I was training to be in the Olympics

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.003
- [Kelly] Oh, wow!

00:03:46.003 --> 00:03:47.230
- and that's what I wanted to do.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.540
But then my dad, you know,

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.520
he was playing a lot

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.520
and I loved music.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.640
And next thing you know,

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:52.473
he said, " Well,

00:03:52.473 --> 00:03:54.220
my other percussion player was sick

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.920
so we need to substitute him."

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.753
And I was like,

00:03:57.753 --> 00:03:58.910
I know all the music I could do it,

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.170
and I was 15.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.470
And how old are you now?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.038
- I'm 14. (chuckles)

00:04:03.038 --> 00:04:04.040
- Ah, good, good time.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.160
Yeah, go take it.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.530
I went on tour at 15

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:07.650
and I never came back.
- That's awesome!

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.880
- That was it.
- 15?

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:09.713
- 15.
- Wow!

00:04:09.713 --> 00:04:11.156
- I went on the road.
- Wow!

00:04:11.156 --> 00:04:11.989
- That was it.

00:04:11.989 --> 00:04:12.822
- That would be great.

00:04:12.822 --> 00:04:13.655
- Her mom is in the back right now,

00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:15.043
going "Nope... "(laughs)

00:04:15.043 --> 00:04:16.860
(people clap)

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.802
- I'm gonna tell her that.

00:04:17.802 --> 00:04:19.770
- I know it's unfortunate now

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.410
that we can't even be
on the road right now.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.260
But I agree though

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.820
there is something that's so
interesting about that age.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.410
Even working with people on The Voice,

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.243
like artists,

00:04:27.243 --> 00:04:28.770
it's an interesting age

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:31.750
because you are so bold.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.310
You are unaware of another way to be

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:37.210
and it's such a beautiful
time to create, I think,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.270
and to be around artists your age.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.230
It's a really cool thing.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.020
I think we always think,
"Oh, they're young."

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:43.853
No, I'm like,

00:04:43.853 --> 00:04:46.500
yes, but sometimes they
know way more than you think

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.910
and they know it because
it's innate in them

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.040
and they haven't imitated
anything yet, you know?

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.320
So I want to talk about this

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.870
cause you've got a MasterClass right?

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:54.703
- I do.

00:04:54.703 --> 00:04:56.302
- Yeah, that's huge!
- I know.

00:04:56.302 --> 00:04:57.230
Oh my god!

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.580
So anybody who's at home

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.930
you can go on MasterClass

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:00.780
and you go online

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.773
and you can learn how to play,

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.690
taught by me in a way that
is not ordinary, you know?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.200
Cause I grew up, self-taught,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.530
watching my dad play.
- Yeah.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.840
- So I teach you how to play

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.960
by playing on your lap,

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:12.960
playing on the couch,

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.410
playing in the kitchen

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.010
like you don't have to buy
a bunch of gear, you know.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.010
Don't worry about
spending money, you know.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.660
You got pots and pans in the kitchen,

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:21.590
the spoons, the forks.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:22.510
We played...

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.390
That's how I started.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.970
I played on pots and pans,

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.490
my lap, the couch,

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.710
the table, everything.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:28.900
- Hey, that's a clever.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.200
A lot of people are at home right now

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.033
with nothing to do

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.310
and their dream to learn that.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.080
So that's amazing.
- Thank you.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.250
- Well, thank you again
for playing with us today.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.857
It's such an honor to have you.

